$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure (Table 3): A Schlenk tube
was charged with nickel complexes 1a or 2a (0.1-4 % mmol), anhydrous THF
(3.0 mL), NMP (3.0 mL)and aryl dichlorides (1.0 mmol). To the solution
was added a solution of arylzinc reagent (3.0 mL, 1.0 M in THF) at room
temperature with stirring. After it was stirred at 80 °C for 2-12 hours,
the reaction was ceased by addition of water and several drops of HCl.
Then the mixture was extracted with ethyl acetate (3×5 mL). The combined
organic layer was dried by MgSO4. The filtrate was concentrated by rotary
evaporation and the crude product was purified by column chromatography
on sillca gel to afford the desired product. 2,6-diphenylpyridine, yield
(%) 95 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, TMS): δ 8.16 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 4H), 7.82 (t,
J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.69 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.51 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 4H), 7.44
(t, J = 7.4 Hz, 2H) ppm. MS (EI, m/z): 231 [M+]
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient Negishi Coupling Reactions of Aryl Chlorides Catalyzed by
Binuclear and Mononuclear Nickel-N-Heterocyclic Carbene Complexes
