$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure B: Pd-Catalyzed Negishi
Coupling of Aryl Halides with Secondary Alkylzinc Halides. Procedure A
was used with the following changes: A THF solution of alkyl zinc halide
(1.20 mmol, 1.50-2.50 mL) was slowly added via syringe at room
temperature instead of at 0 °C. Or following general procedure B with
2-chlorobenzonitrile (138 mg, 1.00 mmol) and isopropyl zinc bromide
solution (2.40 mL, 1.20 mmol, 0.500 M in THF), and toluene (1.60 mL) at
room temperature for 3 h, the crude product was purified via the Biotage
SP4 (silica-packed SNAP 10 g; 0-6% ethyl acetate/hexanes) to provide a
mixture of products as a colorless oil (136 mg, 94% yield). The ratio of
the branched to the linear cross-coupled product was determined to be
22:1 by GC and 1H NMR analysis. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ : 7.61 (d, J =
7.5 Hz, 1H), 7.56 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 7.40 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 7.28 (t,
J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 3.39 (septet, J = 6.9 Hz, 1H), 1.32 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 6H)
ppm. 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ : 152.4, 133.1, 132.9, 126.4, 126.0,
118.3, 111.7, 32.5, 23.3 (2C) ppm. IR (neat, cm-1): 2967, 2874, 2223,
1600, 1484, 1465, 1448, 1388, 1367, 1082, 1032, 762, 526.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, catalyst ligand prepared and used, Negishi coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Negishi Coupling of Secondary Alkylzinc Halides with Aryl Bromides and
Chlorides
