$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure B: Pd-Catalyzed Negishi
Coupling of Aryl Halides with Secondary Alkylzinc Halides. Procedure A
was used with the following changes: A THF solution of alkyl zinc halide
(1.20 mmol, 1.50-2.50 mL) was slowly added via syringe at room
temperature instead of at 0 °C. Or following general procedure B with
4-chlorobenzaldehyde (141 mg, 1.00 mmol) and isopropyl zinc bromide
solution (2.40 mL, 1.20 mmol, 0.500 M in THF), and toluene (1.60 mL) at
room temperature for 30 min, the reaction was quenched by saturated
ammonium chloride solution instead of hydrochloric acid (1N). The crude
product was purified via the Biotage SP4 (silica-packed SNAP 10 g; 0-6%
ethyl acetate/hexanes) to provide a mixture of products as a colorless
oil (138 mg, 93% yield). The ratio of the branched to the linear
cross-coupled product was determined to be 47:1 by GC and 1H NMR
analysis. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ : 9.98 (s, 1H), 7.83 (d, J = 8.4 Hz,
2H), 7.39 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 3.00 (septet, J = 6.9 Hz, 1H), 1.29 (d, J
= 6.9 Hz, 6H) ppm. 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ : 192.0, 156.2, 134.6, 130.0
(2C), 127.2 (2C), 34.5, 23.7 (2C) ppm. IR (neat, cm-1): 2964, 2872, 2826,
2733, 1701, 1608, 1576, 1306, 1213, 1170, 1055, 840, 829, 730, 541.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, catalyst ligand prepared and used, Negishi coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Negishi Coupling of Secondary Alkylzinc Halides with Aryl Bromides and
Chlorides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Han, Chong; Buchwald, Stephen L.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2009), 131(22), 7532-7533

