$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the cross-coupling of
aryl iodides and secondary alkylzinc iodides:
1-(sec-butyl)-3,5-dimethylbenzene (Table 2, Row 3, Column 3, Entry 2).
The general procedure was employed with the following modification: ether
used for extractions during work-up. A colorless liquid (149 mg, 92%) was
isolated by column chromatography (97:3 Hex:Ether). 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) δ: 6.86 (s, 1H), 6.83 (s, 2H), 2.54 (app. sextet, J = 7.3 Hz, 1H),
2.33 (s, 6H), 1.61 (m, 2H), 1.24 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H), 0.86 (t, J = 7.3
Hz, 3H) ppm. 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 147.9, 137.7, 127.6, 125.0,
41.7, 31.3, 22.0, 21.5, 12.5 ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective (>100:1 s-Bu product:n-Bu product), Negishi cross-coupling
reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nickel-Catalyzed Negishi Cross-Coupling Reactions of Secondary Alkylzinc
Halides and Aryl Iodides
