$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the cross-coupling of
aryl iodides and secondary alkylzinc iodides:
((4-(sec-Butyl)phenyl)ethynyl)trimethylsilane (Table 2, Row 3, Column 2,
Entry 2). The general procedure was employed with the following
modification: 36 h reaction time. A yellow liquid (215 mg, 93%) was
isolated by column chromatography (95:5 Hex:Ether). 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) δ: 7.39 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 2H), 7.10 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 2H), 2.59 (m,
1H), 1.56 (m, 2H), 1.21 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H), 0.79 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H),
0.24 (s, 9H) ppm. 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 148.5, 132.0, 127.1, 120.5,
105.5, 93.3, 41.8, 31.1, 21.8, 12.3, 0.2 ppm. IR (neat, cm-1): 3081,
3028, 2961, 2929, 2875, 2158, 1501, 1460, 1250, 842, 900, 760. Anal.
Calcd. for C15H22Si: C, 78.19; H, 9.62. Found: C, 77.55; H, 9.45.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective (>100:1 s-Bu product:n-Bu product), Negishi cross-coupling
reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nickel-Catalyzed Negishi Cross-Coupling Reactions of Secondary Alkylzinc
Halides and Aryl Iodides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Joshi-Pangu, Amruta; Ganesh, Madhu; Biscoe, Mark R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2011), 13(5), 1218-1221

