$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Cross-coupling reaction of 3-bromochromones
and arylzinc bromides A hot oven-dried Schlenk tube was charged with
3-bromochromone (0.5 mmol), NiCl2(PPh3)2 (0.05 equiv, 16 mg, 0.025 mmol),
and LiCl (1.5 equiv, 31.5 mg, 0.75 mmol) followed by THF (2 mL). The
reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 5 min, arylzinc
bromide (1.1 equiv, 0.55 mmol) was added and stirred at room temperature
for one more hour. The reaction mixture was quenched with 10 % HCl (2
mL), and extracted with ethyl acetate (2 × 15 mL). The combined ethyl
acetate extract was washed with 10 % HCl (5 mL), brine (5 mL), and dried
over anhydrous MgSO4. The organic layer was concentrated under vacuum to
give the crude product. Evaporation of the solvent in vacuo and
purification by column chromatography afforded the expected
cross-coupling products. Cross-coupling product c2, Yield: 92%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative preparation shown, Negishi cross-coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of isoflavones by room-temperature nickel-catalyzed
cross-couplings of 3-iodo(bromo)chromones with arylzincs
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zhang, Zunting; Qiao, Jinfeng; Wang, Ding; Han, Ling; Ding, Ru
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Molecular Diversity (2014), 18(2), 245-251

