$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the cross-coupling of
aryl iodides and secondary alkylzinc iodides:
2-(4-(sec-Butyl)phenyl)-4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolane (Table 2,
Row 2, Column 3, Entry 2). The general procedure was employed with the
following modification: 30 h reaction time. A white solid (238 mg, 92%)
was isolated by column chromatography (gradient from 93:7 to 90:10
Hex:EtOAc). Mp: 88-91 ºC. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 7.74 (d, J = 8.5 Hz,
2H), 7.20 (d, J =J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 2.60 (m, 1H), 1.60 (m, 2H), 1.34 (s,
12H), 1.23 (d, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H), 0.81 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H) ppm. 13C NMR (75
MHz, CDCl3) δ: 151.3, 135.0, 126.7, 83.7, 42.1, 31.1, 25.0, 21.9, 12.4
ppm. 11B NMR (160 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 31.0 ppm. IR (neat, cm-1): 3047, 2961,
2930, 2866, 1611, 1460, 1398, 1360, 1323, 1271, 1143, 1107, 1090, 859,
740, 662. Anal. Calcd. for C16H25BO2: C, 73.86; H, 9.69. Found: C, 74.14;
H, 9.64.
