$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the cross-coupling of
aryl iodides and secondary alkylzinc iodides:
((4-iso-Propylphenyl)ethynyl)trimethylsilane (Table 2, Row 3, Column 2,
Entry 1). The general procedure was employed with the following
modification: 42 h reaction time. A yellow liquid (197 mg, 91%) was
isolated by column chromatography (95:5 Hex:Ether). 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) δ: 7.39 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 2H), 7.15 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 2H), 2.89
(septet, J = 6.9 Hz, 1H), 1.23 (d, J= 6.9 Hz, 6H), 0.24 (s, 9H) ppm. 13C
NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 149.7, 132.1, 126.5, 120.6, 105.5, 93.3, 34.2,
23.9, 0.2 ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective (>100:1 i-Pr product:n-Pr product), Negishi cross-coupling
reaction
