$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the cross-coupling of
aryl iodides and secondary alkylzinc iodides:
1-(iso-Propyl)-4-methoxybenzene (Table 2, Row 1, Column 1, Entry 1). The
general procedure was employed with the following modification: ether
used for extractions during work-up. A colorless liquid (138 mg, 92%) was
isolated by column chromatography (95:5 Hex:Ether). 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) δ: 7.17 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 2H), 6.86 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H), 3.81 (s,
3H), 2.88 (septet, J = 6.8 Hz, 1H), 1.25 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 6H) ppm. 13C NMR
(125 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 157.8, 141.2, 127.4, 113.8, 55.4, 33.4, 24.2 ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective (>100:1 i-Pr product:n-Pr product), Negishi cross-coupling
reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nickel-Catalyzed Negishi Cross-Coupling Reactions of Secondary Alkylzinc
Halides and Aryl Iodides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Joshi-Pangu, Amruta; Ganesh, Madhu; Biscoe, Mark R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2011), 13(5), 1218-1221

