$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Negishi Cross-Coupling Reaction; General Procedure 2 Halide (10 mmol),
Pd2dba3·CHCl3 (263 mg, 0.25 mmol, 2.5 mol%), dppf (282 mg, 0.5 mmol, 5
mol%), THF (75 mL) and the organozinc reagent solution 1 (14 mmol, 1.4
equiv) were stirred for 24-48 h at 50 °C under argon atmosphere. The
reaction mixture was allowed to cool to 25 °C, quenched with sat. NH4Cl
(20 mL) and extracted several times with EtOAc. The combined organic
phases were washed with H2O (10 mL) and brine (10 mL) and dried (Na2SO4).
After removal of all volatiles, the residue was purified by column
chromatography (Table 2). Ethyl 3-(2-Methoxynaphthalen-1-yl)propiolate
(2) Prepared from 1-iodo-2-methoxynaphthalene (5.67 g, 19.6 mmol) and 1
(94 mL, 23.5 mmol), following General Procedure 2; The spectroscopic data
are in accordance with the published data.16 Yield: 4.54 g (91%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Negishi cross-coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM On the synthesis of arylpropiolic acids and investigations towards the
formation of vinyl chlorides by HCl addition during esterification
reactions
