$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical procedure 2 (TP2): Cross-coupling
reactions of adamantylzinc reagents. The desired aryl halide (0.9 equiv)
was added to the freshly prepared zinc reagent followed by Pd(OAc)2 (1
mol%) and SPhos (2 mol%) and the mixture was stirred for the given time
at 50 °C. The reaction mixture was quenched with sat. NH4Cl solution (10
mL) and extracted with EtOAc (3×20 mL). The combined organic phases were
dried over Na2SO4 and concentrated in vacuo. The crude residue obtained
was purified by flash column chromatography to give the analytically pure
product. Preparation of 5-(adamantan-1-yl)-2-methylbenzothiazole (4l).
The cross-coupling reaction of 2a (3.2 mL, 1.0 mmol, 0.32 M in THF) with
Pd(OAc)2 (2 mg, 0.01 mmol), SPhos (8 mg, 0.02 mmol) and
5-bromo-2-methylbenzothiazole (3n, 205 mg, 0.9 mmol) was performed
according to TP2 in 2 h. Flash column chromatography (silica, EtOAc pur)
furnished 4l as a brown solid (232 mg, 91 %). m.p.: 147.4-149.6 °C. 1H
NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm) = 7.89-8.00 (m, H), 7.73 (d, J=8.6Hz, 1H),
7.40 (dd, J=8.6Hz, 1.9Hz, 1H), 2.82 (s, 3H), 2.12 (bs, 3H), 1.93-2.03 (m,
6H), 1.68-1.87 (m, 6H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm) = 166.8, 153.7,
149.9, 132.5, 122.3, 120.7, 118.6, 43.4, 36.8, 36.3, 29.0, 20.1. MS (70
eV, EI), m/z (%) = 283 (M+, 83), 240 (10), 227 (19), 226 (100), 189 (18),
184 (5), 162 (10). HRMS (EI), m/z calc. for C18H21NS (283.1395):
283.1351. IR (ATR) υ (cm-1) = 3054, 3028, 2954, 2925, 2916, 2901, 2843,
1739, 1526, 1458, 1448, 1415, 1342, 1308, 1260, 1241, 1168, 1160, 1101,
1067, 980, 974, 923, 876, 795, 728, 656.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Negishi reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Substituted Adamantylzinc Reagents Using a Mg-Insertion in
the Presence of ZnCl2 and Further Functionalizations
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Saemann, Christoph; Dhayalan, Vasudevan; Schreiner, Peter R.; Knochel,
Paul
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2014), 16(9), 2418-2421

