$DATUM 109-99-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the cross-coupling of
aryl iodides and secondary alkylzinc iodides: Methyl
4-(iso-propyl)benzoate (Table 2, Row 3, Column 1, Entry 1). The general
procedure was employed with the following modifications: LiBF4 (93.7 mg,
1mmol) was weighed out and added to the reaction vial in a
nitrogen-filled glove box, 5 mol% NiCl2 and terpyridine employed, 40 h
reaction time. A colorless liquid (163 mg, 91%) was isolated by column
chromatography (85:15 Hex:EtOAc). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 7.97 (d, J =
8.7 Hz, 2H), 7.29 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 3.90 (s, 3H), 2.96 (septet, J =
6.8 Hz, 1H), 1.27 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 6H) ppm. 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ:
167.3, 154.4, 129.9, 127.9, 126.6, 52.1, 34.4, 23.8 ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective (>200:1 i-Pr product:n-Pr product), Negishi cross-coupling
reaction, glove box used, optimization study (optimized on additive)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nickel-Catalyzed Negishi Cross-Coupling Reactions of Secondary Alkylzinc
Halides and Aryl Iodides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Joshi-Pangu, Amruta; Ganesh, Madhu; Biscoe, Mark R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2011), 13(5), 1218-1221

