$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the cross-coupling of
aryl iodides and secondary alkylzinc iodides:
1-(iso-Propyl)-3-methoxybenzene (Table 2, Row 2, Column 1, Entry 1). The
general procedure was employed with the following modifications: LiBF4
(93.7 mg, 1mmol) was weighed out and added to the reaction vial in a
nitrogen-filled glove box, 30 h reaction time, ether used for extractions
during work-up. A pale yellow liquid (136 mg, 91%) was isolated by column
chromatography (95:5 Hex:Ether). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 7.23 (t, J =
7.8 Hz, 1H), 6.84 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 6.79 (m, 1H), 6.73 (d, J = 7.8 Hz,
1H), 3.82 (s, 3H), 2.89 (septet, J = 6.8 Hz, 1H), 1.26 (d, J = 6.8 Hz,
6H) ppm. 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 159.8, 150.8, 129.4, 119.0, 112.6,
110.9, 55.3, 34.3, 24.1 ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective (>100:1 i-Pr product:n-Pr product), Negishi cross-coupling
reaction, glove box used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nickel-Catalyzed Negishi Cross-Coupling Reactions of Secondary Alkylzinc
Halides and Aryl Iodides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Joshi-Pangu, Amruta; Ganesh, Madhu; Biscoe, Mark R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2011), 13(5), 1218-1221

