$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the cross-coupling of
aryl iodides and secondary alkylzinc iodides:
1,3-Dimethyl-5-(octan-3-yl)benzene (Table 3, Row 1, Column 3). The
general procedure was employed with the following modifications: 5 mol%
NiCl2 and terpyridine employed, 15 h reaction time, reaction conducted at
80 ºC, ether used for extractions during work-up. A pale yellow liquid
(199 mg, 91 %) was isolated by column chromatography (95:5 Hex:Ether). 1H
NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 6.84 (s, 1H), 6.76 (s, 2H), 2.34 (m, 1H), 2.32
(s, 6H), 1.60–1.68 (m, 2H), 1.52–1.58 (m, 2H), 1.18–1.28 (m, 6H), 0.87
(t, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H), 0.79 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H) ppm. 13C NMR (125 MHz,
CDCl3) δ: 146.3, 137.5, 127.5, 125.7, 47.9, 36.6, 32.2, 29.8, 27.5, 22.7,
21.5, 14.3, 12.4 ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Negishi cross-coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nickel-Catalyzed Negishi Cross-Coupling Reactions of Secondary Alkylzinc
Halides and Aryl Iodides
