$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the cross-coupling of
aryl iodides and secondary alkylzinc iodides:
1-(iso-Propyl)-3,5-dimethylbenzene (Table 2, Row 3, Column 3, Entry 1).
The general procedure was employed with the following modification: ether
used for extractions during work-up. A colorless liquid (133 mg, 90%) was
isolated by column chromatography (97:3 Hex:Ether). 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) δ: 6.87 (m, 3H), 2.87 (septet, J = 6.8 Hz), 2.33 (s, 6H), 1.27 (d,
J = 6.8 Hz, 6H) ppm. 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 150.0, 137.9, 127.6,
124.4, 34.1, 24.2, 21.5 ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective (>100:1 i-Pr product:n-Pr product), Negishi cross-coupling
reaction
