$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the cross-coupling of
aryl iodides and secondary alkylzinc iodides:
1-(sec-Butyl)-4-methoxybenzene (Table 2, Row 1, Column 1, Entry 2). The
general procedure was employed with the following modification: ether
used for extractions during work-up. A colorless liquid (149 mg, 91%) was
isolated by column chromatography (95:5 Hex:Ether). 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) δ: 7.11 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 2H), 6.85 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 2H), 3.80 (s,
3H), 0.9 Hz, 1H), 3.81 (s, 3H), 2.56 (app. sextet, J = 7.1 Hz, 1H), 1.57
(app. pentet, J = 7.4 Hz, 2H), 1.22 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 3H), 0.83 (t, J = 7.4
Hz, 3H) ppm. 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 157.8, 139.9, 128.0, 113.8, 55.4,
41.0, 31.5, 22.2, 12.4 ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective (>100:1 s-Bu product:n-Bu product), Negishi cross-coupling
reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nickel-Catalyzed Negishi Cross-Coupling Reactions of Secondary Alkylzinc
Halides and Aryl Iodides
